## Parse error rate at scale

LIRA canary observed 0/60 parse errors. At 12-slice scale (~700-900
API calls) the question is whether the schema_adapter remained robust.

**Smoke-test finding pre-launch:** discovered LIRA emits double-block
JSON ~5-15% of the time when it self-corrects mid-response. Production
strip_json_fences yields malformed concat → 40% parse error rate.
Schema adapter patched (commit 4892008) to fall back to last-valid
JSON block. Verified 0% parse errors on smoke-test post-fix.

**This run's observed parse rate:** TBD%

## XAUUSD SHORT share replication

F3 saw 22.8% SHORT share with v2 detector. A2 saw 30.8%. The detector
is identical across all three runs (v2), so the SHORT share difference
between F3 and A2 is purely the consequence of v2's structural
classification on different MSO snapshots — they should match at
fleet-level if v2 is deterministic.

LIRA observed share: TBD% — should match A2 to within rounding (same
detector, same data, same prescreen).

